<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo Motor union agrees on 5.7 pct wage increase.</title>
<headline>Daewoo Motor union agrees on 5.7 pct wage increase.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The union of South Korea's Daewoo Motor said it has agreed on a 5.7 percent increase in basic salary for this year, ending 10 days of industrial action.</p>
<p>A union official said more than 60 percent of the 10,000-strong union voted to accept the wage increase.</p>
<p>Union workers began industrial action at the Bupyong plant on July 9, including a full day strike and partial work stoppages.</p>
<p>The union had demanded a 9.7 percent rise in basic salary, while the management offered a 5.45 percent rise.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
